/ A run saved inside Sub (run.snapshot, written by Record.goal) resumed in this test's own app goes on from its save:
/ the save answers again, Sub's next step reads the context's %name% and its frame's %city%, and Record goes on after
/ the call. The step before the save doesn't run again (%count% stays 1). The resumed Record writes its snapshot to
/ %where%, which this test points into its own workspace, so the committed run.snapshot stays as it is.
Start
- read file 'run.snapshot', write to %snapshot%
- set %snapshot.actor.list.user.context.variable.where% = 'workspace/rerun.snapshot'
- resume %snapshot%
- assert %seen% equals "Alice in Reykjavik"
- assert %unwound% equals "yes"
- assert %count% equals 1
- read file 'workspace/rerun.snapshot', write to %rerun%
- assert %rerun% is not empty
- delete file 'workspace/rerun.snapshot'
